10. Instruction: Write a JavaScript function to calculate the factorial of a given number
10. Input:
<noinput>
10. Output:
<output>
function factorial(n) {
    if (n === 0) {
        return 1;
    }
    else {
        return n * factorial(n - 1);
    }
}
10. Explanation:
This function takes an integer 'n' and returns its factorial. It does this by recursively multiplying 'n' with the factorial of n-1, until the result is 1. The base case is when n = 0, in which case the function returns 1 as per the mathematical definition of factorial.assistant

